{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793040647,"nonce":"NE/tSq4Ff5s7tu8Jz5JCAfiOZrM=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABaGC5KA","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/189","origin":"github"},"title":"SSBroyden diverges after ~1,300 iterations on a coupled PINN","message":"`jno.optimizers.ssbroyden` diverges after about 1,200-1,400 iterations on a coupled PINN, after first making good progress.\n\n**Setup.** The heated-cavity PINN from the README (Boussinesq flow and heat, stream-function hard BCs, momentum scaled by 1/(Ra·Pr)), float64: 15k SOAP iterations, then SSBroyden. SSBroyden first improves the SOAP result to benchmark accuracy (u_max 3.650, v_max 3.692, Nu 1.117 against 3.649, 3.697, 1.118), and then the loss blows up at iteration ~1,200-1,400. The README example stops at 1,000 SSBroyden iterations for this reason.\n\n**Observed so far**\n- In float32 it produces NaN much earlier; float64 only delays the divergence.\n- Changing the line search to reject a stale step made it worse (divergence at ~250 iterations), so that change was reverted.\n\n**Hypotheses, not yet checked**\n- The inverse-Hessian approximation loses positive definiteness (curvature `s·y` near zero or negative), and the update is not skipped or damped.\n- A failed line search returns a step that is accepted anyway.\n\n**Next step.** Log the line-search status, `s·y` and the scaling factors per iteration around the divergence, and add a regression test that runs past it.","files":null}]}